candidates.comparison_that_would_overturn:
On the 64 GB M5 Pro (macOS 26.2+), run the same model family at similar bits (MLX 4-bit against GGUF Q4_K_M) on the route's actual fixtures, comparing mlx_lm.server with llama-server on:
- time to first token at the real prompt lengths;
- decode tokens/s;
- peak unified memory;
- answer agreement;
- kill/restart recovery.

Promote mlx-lm if it wins time to first token and memory at equal quality and stays observable through OmniRoute's gen_ai spans. Reject it if llama.cpp Metal matches, since one engine on both hosts avoids a second runtime.

Run one real Claude plus Codex task through the collector-filtered stream and measure:
(a) per claude_code.interaction, the summed claude_code.llm_request tokens equal the per-task Prometheus/Loki deltas, with no isolated collector;
(b) privacy canary: no stored span or span event carries the cwd path, bash_command, file_path, diff or any gen_ai content key;
(c) Badger TTL deletes spans past retention;
(d) RSS and disk over 24 h;
(e) recovery after kill and restart with a non-ephemeral Badger store.

The proposal is overturned in either case:
- Adding prompt.id (a UUID) to the logs allow-list lets Loki answer (a) exactly, and no remaining trace-only question needs a store.
- Grafana Tempo 3.1.0 (local backend) or Phoenix passes (a) to (e) with lower RSS and disk, or answers through the already-deployed Grafana with equal privacy.

This reopens only if a required evaluation cannot be answered by the pinned harnesses, for example scoring a route's actual outputs attached to live traces. Then compare Langfuse v4 self-host with Phoenix on the same collector-filtered OTLP/HTTP stream:
- total RSS and disk of all services over 24 h;
- whether scoring works on content-free spans;
- a privacy canary;
- restart recovery.
